<figure class="text-figure" data-configuration aria-labelledby="configuration-title">
 <figcaption id="configuration-title"><span class="figure-number">Figure 5</span> Rebuilding an index over the old meaning</figcaption>
 <p class="source-text">Source remains: Blue mugs</p>
 <div class="derivation" data-live>
  <div><span class="scene-label">Configuration now derives</span><strong data-derived>blue · mug</strong></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
  <div><span class="scene-label">Stored vector contains</span><strong data-stored>blue · mug</strong></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
  <div><span class="scene-label">GIN keys contain</span><strong data-indexed>blue · mug</strong></div>
 </div>
 <p class="query-check" data-query-state data-live>Fresh request mugs → mug → match</p>
 <p class="step-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">A private configuration uses the English stemmer. Source mugs and request mugs both become mug.</p>
 <div class="player" role="group" aria-label="Figure 5 playback"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span></div><div class="hold" data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <p class="figure-note">An isolated, checked configuration change: its ASCII-word mapping switches from <code>english_stem</code> to <code>simple</code>. This demonstrates stale stored data; it is not a live migration procedure.</p>
 <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><ol><li>English preparation stores blue and mug. A request for mugs matches.</li><li>The mapping changes to simple. Fresh preparation produces blue and mugs, but the stored vector and index still contain mug. The fresh mugs request misses.</li><li>REINDEX reads the stored vector and puts mug back into the index. The miss remains.</li><li>Regenerating the stored vector from source produces mugs. Its index entry changes too, and the fresh query matches again.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-configuration]')){
 stepper(root,{steps:()=>4,draw(step:number){
  root.querySelector('[data-derived]')!.textContent=step===0?'blue · mug':'blue · mugs';
  root.querySelector('[data-stored]')!.textContent=step===3?'blue · mugs':'blue · mug';
  root.querySelector('[data-indexed]')!.textContent=step===3?'blue · mugs':'blue · mug';
  root.querySelector('[data-query-state]')!.textContent=step===0?'Fresh request mugs → mug → match':step===3?'Fresh request mugs → mugs → match':'Fresh request mugs → mugs → no match';
  root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=[
   'A private configuration uses the English stemmer. Source mugs and request mugs both become mug.',
   'Change that configuration’s word mapping to simple. New preparation keeps mugs, but existing stored vectors have not changed.',
   'REINDEX rebuilds GIN from the stored column. That column still says mug, so the fresh mugs query still misses.',
   'Regenerate the stored vector from its source. PostgreSQL updates its index entries as well. Both now contain mugs and the query matches.'
  ][step];
 }});
}
</script>
